        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4fdaffee-a200-53af-b288-f60fb5698ab3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bern, Switzerland, Zürich, Basel, St. Gallen, southern Germany, Alsace, France\n- Organizations: Bern Minster, Swiss Reformed Church\n- People: Huldrych Zwingli, Johannes Oecolampadius, Berchtold Haller, Niklaus Manuel, Joachim Vadian, Martin Bucer\n- Concepts: Swiss Reformed cathedral, Reformed branch of Protestantism\n\nFacts:\n- The Bern Minster is a Swiss Reformed cathedral in the old city of Bern, Switzerland.\n- The Swiss Reformed Church refers to the Reformed branch of Protestantism in Switzerland.\n- The Swiss Reformed Church began in Zürich with Huldrych Zwingli.\n- Within a few years, the Swiss Reformed Church spread to Basel with Johannes Oecolampadius.\n- Within a few years, the Swiss Reformed Church spread to Bern with Berchtold Haller and Niklaus Manuel.\n- Within a few years, the Swiss Reformed Church spread to St. Gallen with Joachim Vadian.\n- The Swiss Reformed Church spread to cities in southern Germany and, via Alsace with Martin Bucer, to France.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
